This is a comprehensive guide to building a full-stack CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) application using **Node.js**, **Express.js**, and **React**, and then deploying it to the cloud.

---

### Part 1: Project Setup

We will create two folders: one for the **Backend** (Server) and one for the **Frontend** (Client).

#### 1. Create the Backend (Node + Express)

Open your terminal:

```bash
mkdir my-fullstack-app
cd my-fullstack-app
mkdir backend
cd backend
```

Initialize the project and install dependencies:

```bash
npm init -y
npm install express cors nodemon
```

*   **express**: The web framework.
*   **cors**: Allows the frontend to talk to the backend.
*   **nodemon**: Automatically restarts the server when you save files.

#### 2. Create the Frontend (React)

Go back to the root folder and create the React app:

```bash
cd ..
npx create-react-app frontend
cd frontend
npm install axios
```

*   **axios**: Makes it easy to send HTTP requests from React to Express.

---

### Part 2: The Backend Code

We need a server that creates "dummy" data (an in-memory array) and allows us to view and delete it.

Open `backend/server.js` and paste this code:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const cors = require('cors');

const app = express();
const PORT = 5000;

// Middleware
app.use(cors()); // Allow frontend to access backend
app.use(express.json()); // Parse JSON bodies

// Dummy Data (In-memory database)
let users = [
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice Johnson', email: 'alice@example.com', role: 'Admin' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob Smith', email: 'bob@example.com', role: 'User' },
    { id: 3, name: 'Charlie Brown', email: 'charlie@example.com', role: 'User' }
];

// --- API ROUTES ---

// 1. GET: Fetch all users
app.get('/api/users', (req, res) => {
    res.json(users);
});

// 2. POST: Add a new user
app.post('/api/users', (req, res) => {
    const { name, email, role } = req.body;
    const newUser = {
        id: users.length + 1,
        name,
        email,
        role
    };
    users.push(newUser);
    res.status(201).json(newUser);
});

// 3. DELETE: Remove a user
app.delete('/api/users/:id', (req, res) => {
    const id = parseInt(req.params.id);
    users = users.filter(user => user.id !== id);
    res.json({ message: 'User deleted successfully' });
});

// Start Server
app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(`Server is running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

